speechtext:
I just wish to say that the section which is before us is composed of two parts; one is the inquiry and the other is the recommendation for payment. So far as the inquiry is concerned I respectfully suggest that if it should ever be considered necessary the power to set it up is already contained under clause 15(1) of the bill, paragraphs (a) and (e) which read as follows:
(a) inquire into and report to the minister upon measures to assist in a sound economic development of the various modes of transport over which parliament has jurisdiction;
(e) inquire into and report to the minister upon possible financial measures required for direct assistance to any mode of transport and the method of administration of any measures that may be approved;
It is also contained under other subclauses of clause 15. I suggest that the real reason why section 329 is in the bill is in order to
January 18, 1987

have a provision in the bill carrying the implication which the minister admitted it carried, namely, that eventually there will be a charge on the treasury tor any losses that may be proven.
